// or: for (n=3; n<=36; n++) if (n % 3 == 0) print n`,marks:3},{q:"What is the difference between break and continue statements?",model:"break exits the loop immediately. continue skips the rest of the current iteration and moves on to the next iteration.",marks:2}]},{name:"Section C (15 marks)",note:"Answer ONE question. Q23 appendix was not in the files, so the Meeting class is reconstructed.",type:"written",questions:[{q:"Q23: BIUST contracted a freelancer to write a Java meeting manager. Every meeting must have a title, date and time but the Meeting class (Appendix A, not included in your files) has no time. (a) Modify Meeting: add a time with accessors and mutators and amend the non-default constructor. (b) Define an ArrayList of Meeting objects and add all the given objects (updated for time). (c) Use the enhanced for loop to find every meeting on 01-03-2018 and change its time to 1800hrs. (d) Use the enhanced for loop to print the details of all meetings.",model:`class Meeting {
